---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import Glossary from "../../components/Glossary.astro";
import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../styles/extended.css";
import HistoryTimeline from "../../components/HistoryTimeline.astro";
import history from "../../data/history.json";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/aspe/aspe3031.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.description}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
  bannerNotice={metadata.bannerNotice}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "Scope" },
        { id: "s3", label: "What Costs Are Included" },
        { id: "s4", label: "Cost Formulas — FIFO, Weighted Average, and Specific Identification" },
        { id: "s5", label: "No LIFO" },
        { id: "s6", label: "Lower of Cost and Net Realizable Value" },
        { id: "s7", label: "Reversal of a Previous Write-Down" },
        { id: "s8", label: "Worked Example — Calculating Weighted Average Cost" },
        { id: "s9", label: "Worked Example — Reversing a Prior Write-Down" },
        { id: "s10", label: "Disclosure Requirements" },
        { id: "s11", label: "Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates" },
        { id: "s12", label: "Relationship to IAS 2" },
        { id: "s13", label: "Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s14", label: "Related Standards" },
        { id: "s15", label: "Glossary" }
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>
  <div class="wrap">



<div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">A thoroughly converged, cost-anchored standard</div><div class="principle">ASPE Section 3031 governs the RECOGNITION and MEASUREMENT of INVENTORIES — GOODS held FOR sale in the ORDINARY course OF business, in the PROCESS of PRODUCTION for SUCH sale, or in the FORM of materials OR supplies to BE consumed in the PRODUCTION process. THE Section is CLOSELY converged with IAS 2 internationally.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Goods held for sale or consumption in the ordinary course of business</div><div class="principle">This Section applies to INVENTORIES generally, EXCLUDING agricultural INVENTORIES and PRODUCTIVE biological ASSETS (governed SEPARATELY by SECTION 3041 — see the COMPANION poster).</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>What Costs Are Included</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Purchase costs, conversion costs, and costs to bring inventory to its present condition</div><div class="text-supporting">THE cost OF inventory COMPRISES all COSTS of PURCHASE (INCLUDING duties and TRANSPORT, net OF trade DISCOUNTS), costs OF conversion (DIRECT labor and a SYSTEMATIC allocation OF production overhead), and OTHER costs INCURRED in BRINGING the inventory TO its PRESENT location and CONDITION.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>Cost Formulas — FIFO, Weighted Average, and Specific Identification</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">A choice among permitted formulas</div><div class="text-supporting">FOR items THAT are ORDINARILY interchangeable, an ENTERPRISE applies FIFO (first-IN, first-OUT) or WEIGHTED average COST, CONSISTENTLY from PERIOD to period. FOR items THAT are NOT ordinarily INTERCHANGEABLE (e.g. UNIQUE, custom-MADE goods), SPECIFIC identification IS used INSTEAD.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>No LIFO</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">LIFO is not a permitted cost formula</div><div class="text-supporting">LIFO (last-IN, first-OUT) is NOT a PERMITTED cost FORMULA under ASPE — CONSISTENT with IAS 2 internationally, but IN contrast to US GAAP, WHICH continues to PERMIT LIFO as ONE of several ACCEPTABLE inventory COST methods.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Lower of Cost and Net Realizable Value</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">A ceiling on carrying value</div><div class="text-supporting">INVENTORY is MEASURED at the LOWER of COST and NET realizable VALUE (the ESTIMATED selling PRICE in the ORDINARY course OF business, LESS estimated COSTS of COMPLETION and estimated COSTS necessary TO make the SALE) — a WRITE-down is RECOGNIZED whenever COST exceeds NET realizable VALUE.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Reversal of a Previous Write-Down</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Permitted where net realizable value recovers, up to original cost</div><div class="text-supporting">WHERE the CIRCUMSTANCES that PREVIOUSLY caused inventory TO be written DOWN below COST no LONGER exist, OR where THERE is clear EVIDENCE of an INCREASE in NET realizable VALUE, the WRITE-down is REVERSED (LIMITED to the EXTENT of the ORIGINAL write-DOWN, so the CARRYING amount NEVER exceeds ORIGINAL cost) — CONSISTENT with IAS 2'S own REVERSAL permission internationally.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Worked Example — Calculating Weighted Average Cost</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Blending purchases at different prices</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: A retailer's weighted average inventory cost</div><div class="wk-body">A company begins the month with 500 units at $12 each ($6,000). It purchases 300 more units at $14 each ($4,200) during the month.</div><div class="wk-answer">WEIGHTED average COST per UNIT = ($6,000 + $4,200) ÷ (500 + 300) = $10,200 ÷ 800 = <strong>$12.75 per unit</strong>, APPLIED to ALL subsequent SALES and ENDING inventory VALUATION until the NEXT purchase.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Worked Example — Reversing a Prior Write-Down</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Recovering value, limited to the original cost ceiling</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: A recovering commodity price</div><div class="wk-body">A company's inventory, originally costing $200,000, was written down to a net realizable value of $170,000 in the prior period due to a temporary price decline. By the current period end, prices have recovered, and net realizable value is now $230,000.</div><div class="wk-answer">The company REVERSES the PRIOR write-DOWN, RESTATING the INVENTORY to its ORIGINAL $200,000 COST — <strong>NOT</strong> the FULL $230,000 net REALIZABLE value, SINCE the REVERSAL is CAPPED at the ORIGINAL cost basis.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What Section 3031 requires</div><div class="check-list"><span>Accounting policies adopted, including the cost formula used</span><span>Total carrying amount of inventories, classified appropriately</span><span>Amount of any write-down (and reversal) recognized during the period</span></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgment matters most</div>
<div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Whether items are genuinely interchangeable, determining whether specific identification is required</span></div></div>
<div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Net realizable value, including estimated costs of completion and selling costs</span></div></div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Relationship to IAS 2</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — ASPE Section 3031 vs IAS 2</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Feature</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-warning);">ASPE Section 3031</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-info);">IAS 2</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>LIFO permitted</span><span>NO</span><span>NO — converged</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Write-down reversal</span><span>Permitted, up to original cost</span><span>Permitted, up to original cost — converged</span></div>
</div>
<div class="note">A GENUINELY thoroughly CONVERGED standard, WITH no meaningful SUBSTANTIVE divergence FROM IAS 2 to REPORT.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Where every inventory event lands</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Write-down / reversal</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span> <span class="badge is">IS</span></span><span>Recognized as an expense (or expense reduction) in the period</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Section</span><span>Connection</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Section 3041</span><span>Agriculture — governs agricultural inventories and productive biological assets, outside this Section's scope</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s15"><span class="num">15</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2">
<div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Net realizable value</div><div class="glossary-def">Estimated selling price in the ordinary course of business, less estimated costs of completion and costs necessary to make the sale.</div></div>
<div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;"><div class="glossary-term">Specific identification</div><div class="glossary-def">A cost formula assigning actual, individually tracked costs to items that are not ordinarily interchangeable.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="legend"><div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (ASPE terminology)</div><div class="lrow"><div class="litem"><span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge is">IS</span> Income Statement </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge sre">SRE</span> Statement of Retained Earnings / Statement of Changes in Equity </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge scf">SCF</span> Cash Flow Statement</div></div></div>


</div>
  <section id="history">
    <HistoryTimeline items={history.aspe3031 || []} />
  </section>
</StandardPageLayout>
